# VS Code REST Client: click "Send Request" on each block, top to bottom.
# Fees: ₹20 bike / ₹50 car / ₹100 truck per started hour, first hour minimum.
# (A live demo always shows the 1-hour fee; the 61-min / 3-h cases are in the unit tests with FakeClock.)
@base = http://localhost:3000

### 1. Lot with 2 floors: ground has 1 bike + 1 car slot, first floor has 1 car + 1 truck
# @name lot
POST {{base}}/parking-lots
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "HQ", "floors": [ { "bike": 1, "car": 1 }, { "car": 1, "truck": 1 } ] }

### 2. Availability per floor
GET {{base}}/parking-lots/{{lot.response.body.data.id}}/availability

### 3. Park a car → 201, slot F0-C1 (nearest first)
# @name car1
POST {{base}}/parking-lots/{{lot.response.body.data.id}}/park
Content-Type: application/json

{ "vehicleNumber": "KA01AB1234", "vehicleType": "CAR" }

### 4. Second car → F1-C1 (next floor)
POST {{base}}/parking-lots/{{lot.response.body.data.id}}/park
Content-Type: application/json

{ "vehicleNumber": "KA01AB5678", "vehicleType": "CAR" }

### 5. Third car → 409 "No CAR slot available"
POST {{base}}/parking-lots/{{lot.response.body.data.id}}/park
Content-Type: application/json

{ "vehicleNumber": "KA01AB9999", "vehicleType": "CAR" }

### 6. Same car again, typed differently → 409 "already parked" (number is normalised)
POST {{base}}/parking-lots/{{lot.response.body.data.id}}/park
Content-Type: application/json

{ "vehicleNumber": "ka-01 ab 1234", "vehicleType": "CAR" }

### 7. Bike → F0-B1
POST {{base}}/parking-lots/{{lot.response.body.data.id}}/park
Content-Type: application/json

{ "vehicleNumber": "KA05XY0001", "vehicleType": "BIKE" }

### 8. Second bike → 409: no bike slot, and both car slots are taken (it checked CAR too)
POST {{base}}/parking-lots/{{lot.response.body.data.id}}/park
Content-Type: application/json

{ "vehicleNumber": "KA05XY0002", "vehicleType": "BIKE" }

### 9. Availability now: only the truck slot is free
GET {{base}}/parking-lots/{{lot.response.body.data.id}}/availability

### 10. Unpark car 1 → 200 { fee: 50, durationMinutes, billableHours: 1, ticket: PAID }
POST {{base}}/parking-lots/{{lot.response.body.data.id}}/unpark
Content-Type: application/json

{ "ticketId": "{{car1.response.body.data.id}}" }

### 11. Unpark again → 409 "already paid"
POST {{base}}/parking-lots/{{lot.response.body.data.id}}/unpark
Content-Type: application/json

{ "ticketId": "{{car1.response.body.data.id}}" }

### 12. The second bike now fits... in the freed CAR slot F0-C1
POST {{base}}/parking-lots/{{lot.response.body.data.id}}/park
Content-Type: application/json

{ "vehicleNumber": "KA05XY0002", "vehicleType": "BIKE" }

### 13. The closed ticket
GET {{base}}/tickets/{{car1.response.body.data.id}}

### 14. Bad layout → 400 with nested paths (floors.0.car ...)
POST {{base}}/parking-lots
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "", "floors": [ { "car": -1, "boat": 2 } ] }
